.TH SHB 1 "October 2026" "SecretHarbor 0.4.0-prod" "SecretHarbor Manual"
.SH NAME
shb \- security layer for AI agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBshb\fR [\fIcommand\fR] [\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
SecretHarbor creates an OS-enforced security boundary around AI agents and their child processes.
It protects real secrets (.env, cloud keys, database credentials, SSH private keys) by
transparently virtualizing them with synthetic fakes and isolating network and IPC endpoints.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Initialize SecretHarbor host integration and project policy
.TP
\fBadopt\fR
Discover and adopt unprotected running agents
.TP
\fBrestart\fR
Cleanly restart an agent inside a fresh sandbox
.TP
\fBrun\fR
Explicitly run an agent inside the security boundary (debug/fallback)
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show active protection and enforcement status
.TP
\fBsessions\fR
List active SecretHarbor sessions
.TP
\fBstop\fR
Stop a guarded agent session
.TP
\fBconfig\fR
Inspect and manage effective policy configuration
.TP
\fBpolicy\fR
Policy validation and resource decision explanation
.TP
\fBsecret\fR
Manage credentials and broker capabilities
.TP
\fBenv\fR
Manage environment and live secret updates
.TP
\fBrestore\fR
Restore real secret files from a legacy in-place swap session
.TP
\fBtrust\fR
Manage the advisory trusted process list (not yet enforced)
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Run adversarial security verification test suite
.TP
\fBguard\fR
Enable or explicitly disable protection for this project
.TP
\fBupdate\fR
Check for and install SecretHarbor updates
.TP
\fBversion\fR
Show SecretHarbor version and security subsystem details
.TP
\fBhelp\fR
Show CLI documentation
.SH SECURITY
The agent cannot modify the active SecretHarbor policy or disable its own security boundary.
File operations outside the authorized workspace and unapproved capability escalations are denied by the kernel.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
\fBshb init\fR
Initialize host integration, detect agents, and install persistent launcher shims
.TP
\fBshb adopt\fR
Discover unprotected running agents and restart them under SecretHarbor
.TP
\fBshb restart claude\fR
Cleanly restart Claude Code inside a fresh SecretHarbor sandbox
.TP
\fBshb status\fR
Show host integration, active protected sessions, and unprotected processes
.TP
\fBshb config\fR
Inspect effective configuration without exposing secret values
.TP
\fBshb policy explain .env\fR
Explain why .env is faked or denied
.TP
\fBshb doctor\fR
Run live 18-vector adversarial attack tests
.SH FILES
.TP
\fIsecretharbor.yaml\fR
Project security policy configuration.
.TP
\fI~/.secretharbor/shims\fR
Transparent agent launcher shims.
.TP
\fI~/.secretharbor/vault.enc\fR
AES-256-GCM encrypted local credential vault.
.TP
\fI~/.secretharbor/audit.log\fR
Redacted security audit trail.
.SH SEE ALSO
